          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "असली (aslī) is usually traced to Arabic aṣlī, \"original\", from aṣl, \"a root\", through Persian: the thing itself, not a copy."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
